ations within their four-year window. That is why many boxes start at 0.","Mean versus median: the mean is above the median in 8 of 8 years, because a few highly cited works pull the average up. The widest gap is 2021: mean 0.2, median 0.08, top work 2.25. The median is the better guide to a typical work.","Still counting: works from 2023–2026 have not completed their four-year citation window, so their values will rise. Do not compare them with older years yet.","Small base: the values for 2013–2014 are based on only 10–29 works (lighter box or hollow point), so read them with care.","Few works: 2006 and 2012 have fewer than 10 works (2006: 1, 2012: 4), too few for a box. Each of those works is drawn as a dot."],"citations":["Typical work: works published 2015–2023 have a median of 0–2 citations each; the highest median (2) is in 2016 and 2020.","Most cited works: the top 10% of works published in 2018 have at least 7.2 citations each, the highest P90 in the chart.","Not yet cited: more than half of the works published 2023–2026 have no citations so far. This is expected for recent works and is not a sign of low quality.","Mean versus median: the mean is above the median in 9 of 9 years, because a few highly cited works pull the average up. The widest gap is 2018: mean 3.1, median 1, top work 25. The median is the better guide to a typical work.","Recent years: works from 2024–2026 have had less than three years to be cited, so their values will rise.","Small base: the values for 2013–2014 are based on only 10–29 works (lighter box or hollow point), so read them with care.","Few works: 2006 and 2012 have fewer than 10 works (2006: 1, 2012: 4), too few for a band. Each of those works is drawn as a dot."]}}}